  {
    "number": 389,
    "title": "Record installed Codex CLI and Claude Code session-end observations",
    "body": "Refs #312\n\n## Problem\n\n`docs/provider-qualification.md` listed the Codex CLI and Claude Code session ends as documented only. #241's retirement rule had never been observed on an installed Hub for those two paths.\n\n## Result\n\n- The \"Runtime ends and archive admission\" table now records installed evidence for Codex CLI and Claude Code: normal exit, `/clear` and resume.\n- A new subsection, \"Installed CLI and Claude observation\", gives the setup, the events each client emitted, the owner's removal and recreation per path with owner revisions, and the evidence limits.\n- `docs/session-retirement-compatibility.md` now points to the observation instead of saying it is still needed.\n- The Evidence classes line now says the \"none performed\" note applies to the Hub #2 source delivery.\n\nWhat was observed on the installed Hub 0.3.7 (`68c9333`, Agent State 3.2.0) on 2026-09-25:\n\n- Every observed end retired its session. Every same-ID start after retirement created a fresh record.\n- Claude Code `/clear` starts a new session ID. Resume keeps the ID in both clients.\n- Codex CLI 0.156.0 sends no end at `/clear`. The cleared session ends only when the CLI exits. The owner reviewed this and accepted it as client behavior, with no bug filed (issue checkpoint).\n\n## Scope and installation\n\n- No installation was needed. The installation already ran Hub 0.3.7 with Agent State 3.2.0 from the #330 install, which supersedes the 0.3.5 the story names. The owner approved qualifying 0.3.7 without reinstalling.\n- The Claude Code producer came from #367.\n- No hook, service or device was changed. The only client-state writes were folder trust for the empty session directory in both clients and one dismissed Codex update prompt.\n- The raw observation log and debug logs are private evidence outside Git.\n\n## Validation (at `d5a4592`)\n\n- `npm ci`, then `npm run check:workflow`: exit 0. The inventory is 18 specs with no active changes.\n- `npm run test:workflow`: 15/15 pass.\n- `npm run build` and `npm run test:lifecycle:package:built`: exit 0. The lifecycle package bundles `provider-qualification.md`.\n- This is a documentation-only change with no product behavior delta, so there is no OpenSpec change.\n\n## Remaining completion work\n\n- Independent Standards and Specification reviews.\n- Depot CI.\n- Guarded merge.\n- Main CI readback.\n- An issue comment with the per-path results, then closure of #312.\n\n## Execution record\n\n| Field | Value |\n| --- | --- |\n| Issue | jimmie-potts/agent-device-hub#312 |\n| Recommended | One-shot, sonnet, medium |\n| Coordinator model | claude-opus-5-5 (self-reported) |\n| Coordinator level | medium (user-stated) |\n| Session type | One-shot |\n| Workers | none |\n| Reviewers | none |\n| Agents | 1 |\n| Consultations | not applicable |\n| Review rounds | final 0; task 0 |\n| Findings | P0 0; P1 0; P2 0; P3 0 |\n| Corrections | 0 |\n\n**Recorded:** 2026-09-25, agent-skills@bdff385\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
    "state": "open",
