  {
    "number": 388,
    "title": "Keep the hub starting when its MCP tool catalog grows",
    "body": "## Change\n\n**Problem.** With `\"mcp\": true`, the installed hub would not start once it had six controllers. The shared MCP gateway rejected a tool catalog over its 1 MiB response limit, and the CLI printed only `hub-start-failed`. Every hub client went offline (codex-nanoleaf#167 hit this adding the NL22 Panels).\n\n**Cause.** `packages/mcp` built every tool's output schema from one base that embeds the whole controller-contract `$defs` (about 34 KiB). A service-extension tool can only return `extension` or `gateway-error`, yet it published snapshot, receipt and device-list alternatives plus every definition. Measured on `main` `21583cd`:\n- one Nanoleaf controller: 15 tools and 548 KiB;\n- two Nanoleaf controllers: 915 KiB;\n- a third controller of any kind: over the limit.\n\n**Fix**\n- **`packages/mcp`:**\n  - An extension tool publishes an output schema that allows only `extension` or `gateway-error`.\n  - Every published input and output schema keeps only the shared definitions it references, transitively.\n  - Output validation is unchanged: `checkOutput` still compiles the extension's own schema.\n- **`apps/hub`:** a failed start names a stable, path-free cause, for example `hub-start-failed: invalid-configuration`. A catalog that is too large reports `hub-start-failed: mcp-tool-catalog-too-large`. Other errors keep the bare message.\n- **Docs:** `packages/mcp/README.md` and `apps/hub/README.md`.\n\n**Result.**\n- The owner's set of six controllers (Nanoleaf Lines, Nanoleaf Panels, Pixoo, Tidbyt and two LIFX) starts with MCP on.\n- At the hub's own 16-controller maximum, the catalog is 405 KiB, under half the 1 MiB limit.\n\nRefs #357. **No OpenSpec delta:** this restores the existing `standalone-hub-mcp` behavior (configured controllers are served over MCP) within the `shared-mcp-gateway` finite-response bound. The published output schemas stay accurate descriptions of the results the gateway returns, and no request, result or wire value changes.\n\n**Scope note on acceptance 2 (\"degrades clearly instead of failing startup\").** This takes the issue's own first example, a clear startup error that names the limit. With pruning, the catalog cannot reach the limit within the hub's 16-controller and 256-tool bounds, and the new test proves the controller bound. So I did not add a mode that starts with MCP silently disabled. Revisit trigger: raising either bound.\n\n## Validation\n\nAll commands ran from the worktree with Node 24 (`fnm exec --using=24`) and `TMPDIR` outside the checkout, because hub storage refuses a directory inside a checkout.\n\n- **Red first:**\n  - `packages/mcp/tests/tools.test.mjs`: the new \"published schemas carry only referenced definitions…\" test failed (29 tests, 1 failure: unpruned `$defs` on `fixture_status`).\n  - `apps/hub/tests/mcp.test.mjs`: the new owner-set test failed with `Tool catalog exceeds response limit`.\n  - `startup-failure.test.mjs` failed because its module did not exist.\n  - After the fix, all of them pass.\n- **Full suite, all exit 0:**\n  - `build`, `typecheck`\n  - `test:contracts` (330 tests), `test:contracts:python`\n  - `test:mcp:built` (29), `test:mcp:protocol:built` (35), `test:mcp:package:built`\n  - `test:hub:built` (123), `test:hub:package:built`, `test:hub:mcp:built` (23)\n  - `check:workflow`, `test:workflow` (15)\n- **Test adaptation:** two existing `protocol.test.mjs` cases set `maxResponseBytes` to \"catalog size + 100\". Now that catalogs are small, that dropped the limit below what their 1,000-character extension result needs, because `boundedJson` counts 6 bytes per character against half the limit. Their limit now has a 16 KiB floor, still at least the catalog plus 100, so they keep testing the envelope case. No assertion changed.\n- **Not run:** the installed-hub check. Re-adding the Panels entry on the installation is codex-nanoleaf#167's step after merge and install.\n\n## Review and CI\n\n- **Base:** `21583cd32a1128e3d0c4f18bcb2f5c6508ede280` (main)\n- **Head:** `034d3ad3473b81e27ae3f83671553d578318ed10`\n- **Merge-base:** `21583cd`\n- **Diff:** `git diff 21583cd...034d3ad`\n- **Worktree:** clean.\n- **Independent reviews:** pending. Two fresh read-only reviewers will cover Standards and Specification.\n- **CI:** pending (Depot `Checks`: workflow, contracts matrix, MCP and dashboard; the work-guide workflow is also triggered).\n\n- UI changes: no.\n\n## Installation impact\n\nSource only. Installing the hub and re-adding `nanoleaf-panels` to `host.json` are separate steps that need the owner's request (codex-nanoleaf#167).\n\n**Follow-up.** Consumers that vendor `device-mcp` 1.0.0, such as the Nanoleaf MCP host, keep the larger schemas until they adopt a release that includes this change.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
